# AIMOS — Cursor rules

Deterministic crypto trading system. Follow these on every task.

## Before starting
- Read `specs/STATUS.md` (what's built / dormant / next) and the top of
  `CHANGELOG.md` (most recent work).
- Design/behavior → `specs/ARCHITECTURE.md` (the build contract; §N sections).
- Run/deploy/config → `specs/OPERATIONS.md`.
- Don't re-implement ✅ items; don't enable 🟡 items without their prerequisite;
  prefer the next ⏭️ item.

## After finishing (mandatory)
- Add a `CHANGELOG.md` entry under *Unreleased* for what you did.
- Update `specs/STATUS.md` if the build state changed; update `specs/OPERATIONS.md`
  for any new flag/env/run mode.
- Pass: `python -m pytest`, `python scripts/check_magic_numbers.py`,
  `python scripts/check_no_naive_datetime.py`, `lint-imports`.

## Hard rules
- Layers (`observation → intelligence → execution`) communicate only via pydantic
  contracts; import direction is enforced by import-linter.
- No LLM in the decision path (§15.3) — sensor/explainer only.
- No hardcoded tunables in `aimos/observation|intelligence|execution` (magic-number
  lint); route through config or `aimos/core/normalize`.
- All time via `clock.now()`. Never edit `core/schemas.py` or the evidence registry
  without explicit approval.
- Live trading stays fail-closed (mandate + go-live ladder + boot guard). Secrets
  never logged/journaled/returned to the UI.
